{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Education to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate documents relative to education matters.","BillNumber":"S2615","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J14","Name":"Joint Committee on Education","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14","ResponseDate":"2024-02-02T17:14:17.68"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2615/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, February 8, 2024 -- The committee on Education, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 283) of Anne M. Gobi for legislation relative to school transportation personnel; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 323) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation to create a school resource officer grant program and fund; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 325) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation relative to the screening of prospective school employees for prior investigations into child abuse or sexual misconduct; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 353) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to school safety issues; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 357) of Walter F. Timilty for legislation relative to school safety and security, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2615).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Education be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 283, 323, 325, 353, and 357 relative to education matters.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[]